# Per-path Claude account routing.
#
#   <path-prefix>	<profile-name>
#
# Fields are separated by a TAB, not spaces, so project paths may contain spaces
# (e.g. "Apps & Games"). Do not re-space these lines by hand.
#
# Longest matching prefix wins. A path with no match uses whatever account you
# are globally signed in with (VS Code "Switch account") — nothing is overridden —
# unless a FALLBACK profile is set (claude-account fallback <name>), which stands in
# for the global account machine-wide until you clear it (fallback none).
#
# Only the ACCOUNT changes. Plugins, MCP servers, memory, settings, hooks and
# session history all stay shared from ~/.claude, because only
# CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR is set — never CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR.
#
# Use the PROJECT ROOT, not the src/ folder: a prefix match covers every
# subfolder, so it works whether you open <Project>, <Project>/src, or a
# .code-workspace file living inside <Project>/src.
#
# Blank lines and #-comments ignored. Edit with `claude-account add|pause|switch`
# rather than by hand — those commands validate the file and refuse to write a
# result that lost rules.
#
# Example (the TABs are required):
#
#   /Users/you/work/AcmeCorp	acme
#   /Users/you/work/Side	personal

